#: ../developer/local-accounts.md:24
msgid ""
"In local mode `app.state.gateway` is `LocalModeGateway` "
"(`cloud_agent/accounts/directory.py`). It has the methods the Gateway "
"client has. Identity and admission are answered from this database, and "
"each Gateway-only method is refused with a typed error, without a network"
" call. Every existing owner check therefore reads the local decision: "
"request admission, claims, goal rounds, waiting messages, team approval "
"and ownership transfer, the on-call service account, Profile and team "
"rosters. A local account ID never reaches the Gateway."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/local-accounts.md:33
msgid "Enabling it"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/local-accounts.md:35
msgid ""
"Local mode needs its own database. At startup it binds an empty database "
"to local identity (`agent_local_identity_namespace`). It refuses a "
"database bound to a Gateway issuer, or one that holds owner data without "
"a binding. Gateway mode, in turn, refuses a database bound to local "
"identity. Both checks take the same table lock, so two listeners that "
"start in different modes cannot each bind the database. No setting skips "
"these checks. Moving an existing Gateway-bound database to local accounts"
" is a separate identity migration (phase A3 in the design), and it is not"
" implemented."
msgstr ""

